%% UC2 data-access sequence. Author: Thin Lei Sandi (523K0075).
sequenceDiagram
    actor Staff as Kitchen Staff
    participant View as Kitchen View
    participant HTTP as Kitchen HTTP Controller
    participant Service as Kitchen Service
    participant Repo as Kitchen Repository
    participant DB as SQLite
    participant Notify as Local Notification Simulator
    Staff->>View: Open incoming orders
    View->>HTTP: GET orders with demo actor context
    HTTP->>Service: queue(username)
    Service->>Repo: Resolve staff role and assigned hub
    Repo->>DB: SELECT users and hubs
    Service->>Repo: Read assigned-hub Submitted queue
    Repo->>DB: SELECT orders and item quantities
    HTTP-->>View: Queue and assigned hub
    Staff->>View: Review order
    View->>HTTP: GET order details
    HTTP->>Service: details(username, orderId)
    Service->>Repo: Check role, hub, status; read item/payment snapshots
    Repo->>DB: SELECT orders, items, payments
    HTTP-->>View: Order details or 403/404/409
    Staff->>View: Confirm or Reject with reason
    View->>HTTP: POST decision
    HTTP->>Service: decide(username, orderId, input)
    Service->>Repo: BEGIN IMMEDIATE
    Repo->>DB: Begin write transaction
    Service->>Repo: Resolve role/hub and re-read status
    Repo->>DB: SELECT current staff and order
    alt Unauthorized, no longer Submitted, or invalid reason
        Service->>Repo: ROLLBACK
        HTTP-->>View: Error; no decision saved
    else Valid decision
        Service->>Repo: Record status, decision and notification flag
        Repo->>DB: UPDATE Submitted order; INSERT staff/time/reason
        Repo->>DB: INSERT notification with failed flag
        Service->>Repo: COMMIT
        Service->>Notify: Attempt simulated customer notification
        alt Simulation reports success
            Service->>Repo: Mark notification sent
            Repo->>DB: UPDATE customer_notifications
        else Failure or exception
            Note over Service,DB: Preserve saved decision and failed notification flag
        end
        HTTP-->>View: Saved decision, staff/time and notification outcome
        Staff->>View: Back to incoming orders
        View->>HTTP: GET refreshed queue
        Note over View,DB: Handled order is absent; order/items/payment history remains
    end
